NNAAMMEE
     mmeerrggee — 3-way file merge

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     mmeerrggee [--EEeeppqqVV] [--LL _l_a_b_e_l] _f_i_l_e_1 _f_i_l_e_2 _f_i_l_e_3

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The mmeerrggee program merges changes leading from _f_i_l_e_2 to _f_i_l_e_3 into _f_i_l_e_1.

     The following options are supported:

     --EE      Default merge: see diff3(1) for details.

     --ee      Same as --EE but does not warn about conflicts.

     --LL _l_a_b_e_l
             Specifies labels to be used in place of corresponding file names
             in conflict reports.  May be given up to three times.

     --pp      Print result to standard output.

     --qq      Be quiet about reporting.

     --VV      Print RCS's version number.

EEXXIITT SSTTAATTUUSS
     The mmeerrggee utility exits with one of the following values:

           0       No overlaps.
           1       Overlaps were found.
           2       An error occurred.

EEXXAAMMPPLLEESS
     Using labels:

           $ merge -q -p -L one -L two -L three file1 file2 file3
           <<<<<<< one
           =======
           bar
           >>>>>>> three

SSEEEE AALLSSOO
     co(1), diff(1), diff3(1), rcsmerge(1)

SSTTAANNDDAARRDDSS
     The flag [--AA] has no effect and is provided for compatibility only.

